Standard HTTP headers on all calls

• Authorization: Bearer sk_live_… / sk_sandbox_…
• Content-Type: application/json
• Accept: application/json
• X-Idempotency-Key: <uuid> (optional, prevents duplicates on retries)
Encaminhamento do IP/Origem do Cliente Final (server-to-server)

Quando a sua aplicação chama esta API a partir do seu servidor (axios, curl, python-requests, etc.), o IP e User-Agent capturados pelo gateway são os do seu servidor, não do cliente final. Para que a Zumbo Cloud registe o IP/Origem real do cliente final (essencial para anti-fraude, KYC e relatórios geográficos), envie os seguintes headers opcionais mas recomendados:

• X-Customer-IP: 41.220.xxx.xxx — IP público do cliente final
• X-Customer-User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 … — User-Agent do browser do cliente
• X-Customer-Origin: https://loja.exemplo.co.mz/checkout — URL da página de origem
Alternativa: pode enviar os mesmos valores dentro do body da requisição como customer_ip, customer_user_agent, customer_origin_url. Os headers têm prioridade sobre o body.

http
Copy
POST /api/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer sk_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
Content-Type: application/json
X-Customer-IP: 41.220.15.88
X-Customer-User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15
X-Customer-Origin: https://loja.exemplo.co.mz/checkout
Authentication
All server-side calls use Bearer with the merchant API key (sk_live_… or sk_sandbox_…). Issued at Merchant → Settings → API Keys or via /api-sandbox for tests.

http
Copy
Authorization: Bearer sk_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
Content-Type: application/json
How the key is validated

• The function extracts the token from the header Authorization.
• Computes SHA-256 and compares with merchant_api_keys.key_hash.
• Verifies status = 'active' and the wallet's authorized domain.
• Resolves the merchant_id from the key — do not send it in the path.
Never expose the secret key in client code. For the browser only use session_token issued by /payment-session.
merchant_id & wallet_code
The whole integration uses only two public identifiers. The internal wallet_id never needs to be sent.

merchant_id
Merchant UUID. Available in Settings → API.

wallet_code
Public 5-digit wallet code (e.g.: 12345).

Payment Flow
Single flow regardless of payment method — server-to-server, with synchronous confirmation (M-Pesa) or asynchronous via callback/webhook (e-Mola, mKesh, cards).

1
POST /payment-orchestrator
Server-to-server: send merchant_id + wallet_code + payment_method + amount + phone (mobile money) or return_url (cards).

2
Gateway response
M-Pesa: synchronous confirmation (success). e-Mola/mKesh: pending → callback. Visa/MC and PayFast: return checkout_url to redirect customer to Debito Pay green Hosted Checkout.

3
Confirmation
Mobile money credits the wallet directly via callback. Cards (Visa/MC and PayFast) are processed in Debito Pay Hosted Checkout and credit the wallet via ledger_transactions after confirmation.

4
Merchant webhook
The webhook-receiver fires payment.completed / payment.failed event to your URL.

