Webhooks
Events sent to the URL configured in Settings → Webhooks. Mandatory HMAC-SHA256 validation with the webhook secret. Automatic retries with exponential backoff up to 24h.

Events fired
Event	Description
payment.completed	Payment confirmed and credited to wallet
payment.failed	Payment declined or expired
payment.refunded	Payment refunded (Visa/MC)
payment.chargeback	Chargeback received (Visa/MC)
json
Copy
{
  "event": "payment.completed",
  "data": {
    "payment_id": "uuid-pending-payment",
    "merchant_id": "MERCHANT_UUID",
    "wallet_code": "12345",
    "amount": 150,
    "currency": "MZN",
    "method": "mpesa",
    "reference": "DD55JOL0XYT",
    "paid_at": "2026-04-18T12:02:15Z"
  },
  "timestamp": "2026-04-18T12:02:16Z"
}
javascript
Copy
import crypto from "crypto";

function verifyWebhook(rawBody, signature, secret) {
  const hash = crypto.createHmac("sha256", secret).update(rawBody).digest("hex");
  return hash === signature;
}
Webhook best practices

• Reply HTTP 200 in less than 5 seconds — otherwise we retry.
• Always validate the signature in the x-webhook-signature header.
• Handle each payment_id idempotently — events may be delivered more than once.
• Configure multiple webhook URLs (production + staging) in Settings → Webhooks.
Error Codes
Standard response for errors — always with explicit success and error fields.

json
Copy
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "INVALID_API_KEY"
}
Status	Code	When it occurs
400	Missing required fields	payment_method, merchant_id or amount missing
400	Invalid amount	Amount below the method's minimum
400	Unsupported payment method	payment_method not recognized
401	INVALID_API_KEY	Bearer missing or hash doesn't match merchant_api_keys
403	WALLET_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLOWED	Origin differs from wallet's allowed_domain
404	WALLET_CODE_NOT_FOUND	wallet_code does not exist
429	Rate limit exceeded	More than 60 sessions/min for the same merchant
500	Internal server error	Gateway/upstream failure
Sandbox
